%[text] # ADS-B Prediction Pipeline Stage Review
%[text] This Live Script is the current educational review artifact for the ADS-B prediction-step experiment. It explains what each completed phase did, what was trained, what was only scored, and why the current data does not yet support a broad neural-model quality claim.
projectRoot = fileparts(mfilename("fullpath"));
addpath(projectRoot);
if ~exist("enableInteractiveGlobe", "var")
    enableInteractiveGlobe = true;
end
review = helperBuildStageReviewArtifacts("ProjectRoot", projectRoot);
trainingDetails = helperBuildStageReviewTrainingDetails(review);
trackDiagnostics = helperBuildStageReviewTrackDiagnostics(review);
selectedTrackHex = trackDiagnostics.easyTrackHex;
turnDiagnosticTrackHex = trackDiagnostics.turnDiagnosticTrackHex;
mlpDiagnostics = helperBuildStageReviewMLPDiagnostics(review, "TrackHex", selectedTrackHex);
phaseSummary = review.phaseSummaryTable %[output:2fa35e95]
metricComparison = review.metricComparisonTable %[output:11f5aa2f]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 2B Data And Smoke Training
%[text] Stage 2B converted local ADS-B truth into adjacent state pairs in Sensor Fusion order |\[x, vx, y, vy, z, vz\]|. It also trained a small MLP in MATLAB, not Python. This was a software plumbing check: the split, normalization, network output shape, loss, and positive variance transform were tested, but the model is not a useful predictor yet.
stage2BDatasetSummary = table( ... %[output:group:2e801a13] %[output:3c5be97b]
    ["usable pairs"; "aircraft tracks"; "median dt [s]"; "constvel position RMSE [m]"; "smoke MLP position RMSE [m]"], ... %[output:3c5be97b]
    [ ... %[output:3c5be97b]
        review.dataset.buildSummary.usablePairCount; ... %[output:3c5be97b]
        review.characterization.diversityAssessment.aircraftCount; ... %[output:3c5be97b]
        review.dataset.buildSummary.dtSummary.median; ... %[output:3c5be97b]
        review.dataset.baselineConstVelMetrics.positionRMSEMeters; ... %[output:3c5be97b]
        review.trainingSummary.modelPositionRMSEMeters], ... %[output:3c5be97b]
    'VariableNames', ["metric", "value"]) %[output:group:2e801a13] %[output:3c5be97b]
%%
%[text] ## NN Training Details
%[text] The training code is |trainLocalADSBMLPSmoke.m|. The saved artifact is loaded from |artifacts/stage2B/localADSBMLPSmokeTraining.mat|. There is no classification accuracy because this is regression; the end-of-run quality indicators are loss, RMSE, and empirical covariance coverage. The validation split exists, but this smoke run did not use it for early stopping or model selection.
trainingScriptPath = fullfile(projectRoot, "trainLocalADSBMLPSmoke.m") %[output:92c08a82]
trainingDetails %[output:4740c24d]
%%
%[text] ## Why The Smoke MLP Line Goes The Wrong Way
%[text] The Stage 2B smoke MLP line is not a plotting artifact. It is the actual saved smoke MLP output. On the easy track below, |constvel| is within meters, while the smoke MLP predicts points tens of kilometers away. This happened because the model only ran a tiny smoke-training pass and its normalized outputs collapsed toward a low-spread dataset-level prior instead of learning the one-step aircraft motion.
mlpDiagnosis = mlpDiagnostics.diagnosisText %[output:2e4ccfe7]
selectedTrackSplitSummary = mlpDiagnostics.splitSummary %[output:7d678eac]
mlpExamplePredictions = mlpDiagnostics.examplePredictionTable %[output:0ac71ef6]
mlpNormalizedSpread = mlpDiagnostics.normalizedSpreadTable %[output:0772dbf3]
mlpLossHistory = mlpDiagnostics.lossHistoryTable %[output:0d31bfd6]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3A Delta-Target MLP
%[text] Stage 3A trains the MLP on state deltas and reconstructs the next state as |previousState + predictedDelta|. The neural input stays motion-focused: velocity, local altitude, elapsed time, covariance diagonal for interface compatibility, and physics-derived delta features. Absolute horizontal |x| and |y| are not default neural features.
if review.hasStage3A %[output:group:0146220d]
    stage3TrainingScriptPath = fullfile(projectRoot, "trainLocalADSBMLPStage3.m") %[output:2fda47f0]
    stage3TrainingReportPath = fullfile(projectRoot, "artifacts", "stage3", "stage3LocalADSBMLPTrainingReport.md") %[output:1cc226e0]
    stage3MetricComparison = review.metricComparisonTable %[output:97273bb1]
    stage3HeadlineRMSE = review.metricComparisonTable( ... %[output:57038428]
        ismember(review.metricComparisonTable.method, ["constvel baseline", "Stage 3A delta MLP"]), ... %[output:57038428]
        ["method", "positionRMSEMeters", "velocityRMSEMetersPerSecond"]) %[output:57038428]
    stage3TrainingLadder = review.stage3Summary.trainingLadder.ladderTable %[output:867f55a7]
    stage3FeatureAblation = review.stage3Summary.trainingLadder.featureAblationTable %[output:42226885]
    stage3ManeuverMetrics = review.stage3Summary.metrics.byManeuverClass %[output:7707c982]
else
    stage3Status = "No Stage 3A training artifact found. Run trainLocalADSBMLPStage3.m to populate this section."
end %[output:group:0146220d]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3A Constvel Versus Delta MLP Error
%[text] This plot focuses only on the native |constvel| comparator and the Stage 3A delta-target MLP for the selected review track. The top panel is row-wise one-step 3D position error. The lower panel is cumulative position RMSE through each timestep, which makes the trend easier to compare.
if review.hasStage3A %[output:group:424dfcf4]
    stage3TrackErrorComparison = helperPlotStageReviewStage3ErrorComparison( ... %[output:035b61b6] %[output:6fbfce62]
        review, ... %[output:035b61b6] %[output:6fbfce62]
        "TrackHex", selectedTrackHex, ... %[output:035b61b6] %[output:6fbfce62]
        "MaxPairs", 80) %[output:035b61b6] %[output:6fbfce62]
else
    stage3TrackErrorComparison = table( ...
        "Stage 3A artifact missing", ...
        NaN, ...
        NaN, ...
        NaN, ...
        'VariableNames', ["method", "trackPositionRMSEMeters", "trackMedianPositionErrorMeters", "trackP95PositionErrorMeters"])
end %[output:group:424dfcf4]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3B Aggregate ADS-B Evaluation
%[text] Stage 3B freezes the Stage 3A network and compares it with native |constvel| on every eligible local ADS-B state pair that can be aggregated from the capture tree. This is an evidence and data-readiness gate, not a retraining run.
if review.hasStage3B %[output:group:9270b862]
    stage3BEvaluationScriptPath = fullfile(projectRoot, "runStage3BAggregateADSBEvaluation.m") %[output:912a28c1]
    stage3BEvaluationReportPath = review.stage3BSummary.reportPath %[output:6e0af509]
    stage3BAggregateRMSE = review.stage3BMetricComparisonTable %[output:0fed1c4b]
    stage3BRecommendation = review.stage3BDataReadiness.recommendation %[output:8c774947]
    stage3BDataReadiness = review.stage3BDataReadiness.gateTable %[output:7524f964]
    stage3BSourceInventory = review.stage3BSummary.inventoryTable %[output:66def45e]
    stage3BFigurePaths = struct2table(review.stage3BSummary.figurePaths, "AsArray", true) %[output:302cc71e]
else
    stage3BStatus = "No Stage 3B aggregate evaluation artifact found. Run runStage3BAggregateADSBEvaluation.m to populate this section."
end %[output:group:9270b862]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3B Track-Level Diagnostics
%[text] These rows help identify whether the frozen Stage 3A MLP is consistently worse than |constvel| or whether the error is concentrated in specific aircraft tracks or update regimes.
if review.hasStage3B %[output:group:2afe5b93]
    stage3BTopTracks = review.stage3BTrackSummary(1:min(8, height(review.stage3BTrackSummary)), :) %[output:1b581e14]
    stage3BManeuverMetrics = review.stage3BSummary.metrics.byManeuverClass %[output:6cc5af7d]
    stage3BDtRegimeMetrics = review.stage3BSummary.metrics.byDtRegime %[output:1f4d4539]
else
    stage3BTopTracks = table( ...
        "Stage 3B artifact missing", ...
        NaN, ...
        'VariableNames', ["status", "value"])
end %[output:group:2afe5b93]
%%
%[text] ## Raw ADS-B Tracks In Local Coordinates
%[text] These are the ADS-B-derived next-state positions in the local east-north-up frame. This plot shows the single-session nature of the current artifact before comparing any model output.
helperPlotStageReviewLocalTracks(review, "MaxTracks", 8); %[output:9c90c89b]
%%
%[text] ## What The Stage 2C Labels Mean
%[text] The labels are not produced by the neural network and are not a classification layer. They are offline diagnostic labels computed from each observed ADS-B state pair: heading change comes from velocity direction, speed change comes from horizontal speed magnitude, vertical-rate change comes from |vz|, climb/descent comes from |vz|, and sparse update comes from |dtSeconds|.
labelRules = review.labelRuleSummaryTable %[output:689384b6]
maneuverCounts = review.maneuverCountsTable %[output:42e24e5a]
%%
%[text] ## Maneuver Coverage And Baseline Error
%[text] The current artifact is dominated by |constvel\_like| behavior. The small |constturn\_like| count is why Stage 2C says we do not yet have enough turn/acceleration/climb diversity for broad learned-model claims. The error histogram uses |log10(position error)| because the smoke NN error is orders of magnitude larger than |constvel|.
helperPlotStageReviewManeuverSummary(review); %[output:8883453d]
%%
%[text] ## Track Selection For Review
%[text] The easy review track is selected from tracks with at least 40 pairs and at least 70 percent |constvel\_like| labels, then sorted by lowest median |constvel| position error. The separate turn diagnostic track is kept for later maneuver inspection, but it is not the default teaching example.
trackSelectionNote = trackDiagnostics.selectionNote %[output:206d8f14]
selectedTrackHex %[output:2f6d068d]
turnDiagnosticTrackHex %[output:7f71577d]
topTrackDiagnostics = trackDiagnostics.trackTable(1:min(8, height(trackDiagnostics.trackTable)), :) %[output:23153cb1]
%%
%[text] ## One Easy Track: ADS-B Truth, Constvel, Smoke NN, And Stage 3A
%[text] - Green is ADS-B-derived next-state truth
%[text] - Blue is native |constvel|, gray is the saved Stage 2B smoke MLP, and red is Stage 3A when the artifact exists
%[text] - Gray smoke-MLP excursions are retained as a reminder that Stage 2B was only a plumbing check \
helperPlotStageReviewPredictionComparison(review, "TrackHex", selectedTrackHex, "MaxPairs", 80); %[output:9c413b7a]
%%
%[text] ## Interactive Globe Review
%[text] The globe overlays ADS-B truth, native |constvel| prediction, the saved smoke NN prediction, and Stage 3A when the artifact exists. Green is truth, blue is |constvel|, gray is the smoke MLP, and red is Stage 3A. Set |enableInteractiveGlobe = false| before running this script to skip the UI section during automated checks.
if enableInteractiveGlobe %[output:group:4a8318d0]
    globeOutput = helperOpenStageReviewGlobe(review, "TrackHex", selectedTrackHex, "MaxPairs", 80);
    globeLegend = globeOutput.legendTable %[output:5505e388]
    viewer = globeOutput.viewer;
    shot1 = snapshot(viewer);
    figure; %[output:368b857a]
    imagesc(shot1); %[output:368b857a]
    axis image; %[output:368b857a]
    xlabel("Snapshot image column"); %[output:368b857a]
    ylabel("Snapshot image row"); %[output:368b857a]
    title("trackingGlobeViewer Snapshot: Truth, Constvel, Smoke MLP, And Stage 3A"); %[output:368b857a]
else
    globeTrajectory = ["ADS-B next-state truth"; "constvel prediction"; "smoke MLP prediction"];
    globeColor = ["green"; "blue"; "gray"];
    if review.hasStage3A
        globeTrajectory = [globeTrajectory; "Stage 3A delta MLP prediction"];
        globeColor = [globeColor; "red"];
    end
    globeLegend = table( ...
        globeTrajectory, ...
        globeColor, ...
        'VariableNames', ["trajectory", "color"])
end %[output:group:4a8318d0]
%%
%[text] ## Current Interpretation
%[text] The native |constvel| model is still the meaningful floor. Stage 3B makes the next decision explicit: keep the Stage 3A model frozen, score it honestly against |constvel|, and only consider retraining after the aggregate data-readiness gate passes.
if review.hasStage3B
    finalInterpretation = review.stage3BDataReadiness.recommendation
else
    finalInterpretation = review.characterization.diversityAssessment.directAnswer
end

